  "summary": "Cedar Rapids police held a Q&A meeting about replacing the city's 70 Flock ALPR cameras with Axon cameras at an annual cost of $98,415. Residents raised Fourth Amendment and oversight concerns, while police described a 30-day retention policy and law-enforcement-purpose search requirement.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I believe that what they are planning and what they are doing violates everyone's Fourth Amendment rights",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "Police say the cameras capture license plates, not faces, and the data is kept for 30 days.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "We know that the public wants safeguards for this kind of technology. We have guidelines in place to make sure that that is successful",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
